codex
The structural equality derivation covers closures, syntax trees, maps, lists, tuples, sets, dictionaries, and nested values—not just the theorem’s integer path. Compilation is slower because the generated Klean universe is one large mutual datatype, but it removes the main semantic shortcut risk in `applyCmp`.
